# KS-1364 analytics-reports - POST /api/analytics/reports publishes a REQUIRED request body

File: `Blockchain/Dev/services/analytics/src/analytics.openapi.ts`  (product, modified in place: one one-line replacement, `:926`)
Test file: `Blockchain/Dev/services/analytics/src/__tests__/ks1364-analytics-reports-body-required.test.ts`  (NEW, 40 lines)
Tip: `723dc0722b68482a03de8577fdb5eb5b3359e725` (origin develop, `git ls-remote` 2026-10-01 09:47 AEST, the base Wednesday named at 09:15). `analytics.openapi.ts` there is 1130 lines.
Runner: `vitest` (analytics service, `vitest run`, `vitest.config.ts` with `globals: true`, environment `node`)

Written 2026-10-01 10:02 AEST by a Spark brief-writer sub-agent for Wednesday, from `723dc0722b68`, `analytics.openapi.ts` read at every line named here and the handler(s) read. Source: KS-1364 (Backlog, assigned to Kamil; created by Peter 2026-09-28 with the sweep-4 evidence): "One for the spec when convenient". Carve: this brief takes `POST /api/analytics/reports` from the ticket's 17-operation table.

## The mode - read this twice

CODE+TEST. Your diff touches EXACTLY 2 files, in this order:
1. `Blockchain/Dev/services/analytics/src/analytics.openapi.ts` - modified in place, `--- a/Blockchain/Dev/services/analytics/src/analytics.openapi.ts` / `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/analytics/src/analytics.openapi.ts`, EXACTLY the 1 hunk(s) given below, byte for byte.
2. `Blockchain/Dev/services/analytics/src/__tests__/ks1364-analytics-reports-body-required.test.ts` - a NEW file: `--- /dev/null` then `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/analytics/src/__tests__/ks1364-analytics-reports-body-required.test.ts`, ONE hunk `@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@`, every line `+`.

You never touch any other file. The `reference_test_file` in your input (the security service's KS-747 spec test) is shape reference only - do NOT touch it.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

The registration for `POST /api/analytics/reports` (`analytics.openapi.ts:919`-`:944`) declares its request body as `body: { content: { 'application/json': { schema: ReportRequestSchema } } }` (`:926`) with no `required`, so the published spec says the body is OPTIONAL. The handler says otherwise: `routes/analytics.ts:388` (`router.post('/reports', ...)`) runs `ReportRequestSchema.parse(req.body)` (`:390`) and maps a `ZodError` to 400 (`:397`-`:401`). That runtime schema (`types/analytics.types.ts:476`) is a `z.object` requiring `type` and `period`, and the spec component this file registers says the same (`analytics.openapi.ts:525` on, KS-430 comment: "requires BOTH"). So an absent body is always a 400. KS-1364's sweep 4 measured exactly that: Schemathesis sent no body and got 400 (1 case, `positive_data_acceptance`, "not baselined"). The ticket's direction is verbatim: "mark `requestBody.required: true` where the handler's Zod schema rejects an absent body, at the generator (`*.openapi.ts`)". The one-line form `body: { content: { ... } }, required: true },` is the house form already used at `governance.openapi.ts:736`.

## Where

- `:926` - **the `/api/analytics/reports` request body has no `required`; it must say `required: true`** (must change)

## The exact change

ONE hunk, a one-line replacement in place (old side 7, new side 7). The line keeps its leading four spaces and gains `, required: true` after the `content` object's closing brace, before the body's own closing ` },`. Every context line is non-blank; the last trailing context line is a comment that contains a section sign and an em dash - copy it byte-exact.

